'''Tyroler''' (ti-rō′lėr), ''n.'' [< G. ''Tyroler'', ''Tiroler'', a Tyrolese, < ''Tyrol'', ''Tirol'', Tyrol: see ''Tyrolese''.] A native of Tyrol; a Tyrolese. [Rare.]

'''Tyrolese''' (tir-ō-lēs′ or -lēz′), ''a.'' and ''n.'' [< ''Tyrol'' (G. ''Tirol'', and improperly ''Tyrol'') + ''-ese''.] '''I.''' ''a.'' Of or pertaining to Tyrol (often called the Tyrol), an Alpine province forming with Vorarlberg a crownland of the Cisleithan division of Austria-Hungary.

'''II.''' ''n. sing.'' and ''pl.'' A native or the natives of Tyrol.
